# Cline Rules - Workspace Rules

## Project Context
- This is a Next.js portfolio website with React, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS
- The project uses Vite for the client-side app
- Includes server-side components with Express/Node.js
- Uses Playwright for testing
- Deployed on AWS Amplify with GitHub integration

## Code Style & Standards
- Use TypeScript for all new code
- Follow existing ESLint and Prettier configurations
- Use functional components with hooks in React
- Follow the existing component structure in `client/components/`
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling (as configured in tailwind.config.ts)
- Implement proper error boundaries for Next.js components
- Use Next.js Image component for optimized images
- Follow Next.js routing conventions

## API & Integrations
- Anthropic Claude API (claude-3-haiku/sonnet/opus)
- OpenAI API (GPT-4, GPT-4o-mini)
- Builder.io for CMS
- GitHub API integration
- AWS services (Lambda, API Gateway, Secrets Manager)
- reCAPTCHA for forms
- Next.js API routes for server-side functionality

## Testing Requirements
- Run Playwright tests before committing significant changes
- Use the existing test structure in `playwright-tests/`
- Include accessibility tests for new components
- Implement unit tests for components and utilities
- Run integration tests for API routes
- Generate test coverage reports

## Security Guidelines
- Never commit API keys or secrets to version control
- Use environment variables for sensitive data
- Follow AWS security best practices
- Implement proper input validation on all endpoints
- Use Next.js security headers and middleware
- Validate all API route inputs
- Implement proper CORS configuration

## Deployment
- Main branch deploys to production automatically via Amplify
- Use feature branches for development
- Check deployment status after pushing to main
- Run pre-deployment checks and tests
- Monitor deployment health and performance

## Next.js Best Practices
- Use `getStaticProps` for static content
- Implement `getServerSideProps` for dynamic content
- Enable incremental static regeneration where appropriate
- Optimize images with Next.js Image component
- Implement proper SEO with metadata
- Use dynamic imports for code splitting
- Follow accessibility guidelines (WCAG)

## Performance Optimization
- Monitor Core Web Vitals metrics
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Optimize bundle size and dependencies
- Use lazy loading for non-critical components
- Implement image optimization
- Monitor and optimize API response times

## Hooks & Automation
- Use cline-hooks for automated workflows
- Implement Next.js-specific hooks for build optimization
- Use skills for common development tasks
- Automate testing and deployment workflows
- Monitor and report on workflow health

## Skills Integration
- Use Next.js development skills for component creation
- Implement API route creation skills
- Use optimization skills for performance improvements
- Leverage testing skills for comprehensive test coverage
- Apply security skills for vulnerability scanning

## Workflow Management
- Use automated CI/CD workflows for builds and deployments
- Implement security scanning workflows
- Run performance optimization workflows
- Monitor workflow execution and health
- Generate workflow reports and metrics
